mutant: m052_pds_cursor_leads_completion
target: internal/ingest/backfill/completion_batcher.go
failure-mode: |
  A per-PDS listRepos cursor treats a still-queued completion as though it were
  already absent/durable. The cursor can therefore commit in an earlier synced
  Pebble batch than the repo completion and its segment rows. A crash in that
  window resumes after the DID and silently loses its archive data.
expected-detection: |
  The pdsbackfill tier's
  TestCompletionBatcherHostCursorNeverLeadsCoveredCompletion holds a covered
  completion below the writer durability boundary and requires both the
  completion and cursor to remain unstaged. The mutant stages the cursor and
  fails immediately. The default oracle remains the end-to-end backstop.
expected-tier: pdsbackfill
tiers: pdsbackfill

